msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-copy-setter.md:17
msgid ""
"// Simplified. \"/home/me/mortgage.pdf\".with_extension(\"mov\") =>\n"
"    // \"/home/me/mortgage.mov\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-copy-setter.md:25
msgid ""
"`with` can be used for methods that copy a value, but then change a specific "
"part of that value."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-copy-setter.md:28
msgid ""
"In the example here, `with_extension` copies the data of a `&Path` into a "
"new `PathBuf`, but changes the extension to something else."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/with-copy-setter.md:31
msgid "The original `Path` is unchanged."
msgstr ""
